1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:05,086
Over high mountains and across valleys

2
00:00:05,447 --> 00:00:08,653
A ninja flies freely in the sky like a plane

3
00:00:08,905 --> 00:00:12,338
Upright and kind, Hattori-kun brings joy to all

4
00:00:12,492 --> 00:00:15,672
With eyes open round and little mouth held tight

5
00:00:16,005 --> 00:00:19,406
Hiding his face, cheeks puffing up

6
00:00:19,572 --> 00:00:22,730
Catching villains with nimble moves fast as lightning

7
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:26,497
Catching bad guys with strange tricks like playing magic

8
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:29,876
Speaking like poetry, polite and spirited

9
00:00:31,813 --> 00:00:34,279
"Don't Drink Too Much"

10
00:00:41,763 --> 00:00:44,684
Dad, hurry up and get up, breakfast is ready

11
00:00:44,724 --> 00:00:46,965
Manager, oh Manager, please spare me

12
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:48,286
I can't drink any more

13
00:00:48,326 --> 00:00:50,767
I'm not the manager, I'm Kenichi!

14
00:00:50,807 --> 00:00:51,807
Get up!

15
00:00:57,203 --> 00:00:58,383
Put it down first

16
00:00:59,268 --> 00:01:00,898
Aiya... it's so cold...

17
00:01:00,939 --> 00:01:03,060
Oh dear, what should we do? He fell asleep again

18
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,461
Oh no, this is bad

19
00:01:04,501 --> 00:01:06,223
That's it, I know what to do! I have an idea

20
00:01:06,263 --> 00:01:07,885
I know it's bound to work

21
00:01:09,365 --> 00:01:12,485
- One, two...
- One, two, three...

22
00:01:13,207 --> 00:01:16,045
Hey, don't do that, you'll get the blanket wet!

23
00:01:16,718 --> 00:01:18,021
Aiya, heavy rain again!

24
00:01:18,061 --> 00:01:19,281
It's a typhoon, oh no!

25
00:01:19,321 --> 00:01:20,701
I can't take it...

26
00:01:22,959 --> 00:01:25,753
My head hurts so badly

27
00:01:25,975 --> 00:01:27,535
Of course you'd have a headache

28
00:01:27,575 --> 00:01:30,175
Because you came home drunk every single night this week

29
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:32,656
There've been so many work drinks lately, huh

30
00:01:32,696 --> 00:01:35,374
I can't turn people down when it's for my job, you know?

31
00:01:35,782 --> 00:01:37,536
With the way you've been drinking lately

32
00:01:37,576 --> 00:01:39,168
you're bound to get sick sooner or later

33
00:01:39,501 --> 00:01:42,563
You have a point, and I know it too

34
00:01:42,723 --> 00:01:45,217
If you get sick, Dad, what will Mom and I do?

35
00:01:45,257 --> 00:01:47,194
Please come home earlier tonight

36
00:01:47,235 --> 00:01:49,288
Dear, look how much your son cares about you

37
00:01:49,335 --> 00:01:51,334
Go on, promise him, hurry

38
00:01:51,374 --> 00:01:53,481
Anyway, I'll try my best. It's getting late

39
00:01:53,522 --> 00:01:54,942
I have to go to work now

40
00:01:55,211 --> 00:01:57,739
Dad, you forgot something!

41
00:01:57,935 --> 00:01:58,629
Yan...

42
00:01:58,675 --> 00:02:00,609
Dad, you left something behind

43
00:02:02,839 --> 00:02:04,698
Thank you, Hattori-kun

44
00:02:05,345 --> 00:02:07,867
He'll probably be just like yesterday again today

45
00:02:07,907 --> 00:02:08,828
Yan...

46
00:02:08,868 --> 00:02:09,753
Hattori-kun

47
00:02:09,793 --> 00:02:12,231
Is there any way to make Dad hate drinking?

48
00:02:12,271 --> 00:02:13,872
Let me think...

49
00:02:13,912 --> 00:02:15,593
If someone hates drinking

50
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:17,115
they won't drink so much

51
00:02:17,155 --> 00:02:19,717
and won't come home in the middle of the night

52
00:02:19,757 --> 00:02:22,319
Alright, let me think of a way. Yan...

53
00:02:37,791 --> 00:02:40,351
Yan...

54
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:46,090
Yan...

55
00:02:52,677 --> 00:02:54,577
My complexion is better than I thought

56
00:02:54,859 --> 00:02:57,322
That means when I get off work... my complexion will look good

57
00:02:57,362 --> 00:02:58,996
Oh dear, that's no good

58
00:02:59,218 --> 00:03:00,038
Alright

59
00:03:00,091 --> 00:03:01,284
I can drink again tonight!

60
00:03:01,325 --> 00:03:02,250
Yan...

61
00:03:02,477 --> 00:03:04,600
Alright, I'll borrow this painting

62
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:05,483
Yan!

63
00:03:06,122 --> 00:03:08,089
Ninja Transformation Technique!

64
00:03:10,239 --> 00:03:11,319
Huh? Oh no

65
00:03:12,481 --> 00:03:13,776
My complexion looks terrible

66
00:03:13,856 --> 00:03:15,035
Probably from too much socializing

67
00:03:15,075 --> 00:03:16,502
And drinking without moderation

68
00:03:16,735 --> 00:03:18,957
I'd better skip tonight's banquet

69
00:03:20,736 --> 00:03:22,001
Hey, Kentaro Mitsuba

70
00:03:22,041 --> 00:03:24,803
We've got to drink to our hearts' content at our dinner tonight

71
00:03:24,843 --> 00:03:25,956
Well, Manager...

72
00:03:26,266 --> 00:03:27,926
I'm really not looking too good

73
00:03:28,935 --> 00:03:31,039
Looks pretty good to me, take a look

74
00:03:31,081 --> 00:03:33,501
With such good color, how could anything be wrong?

75
00:03:33,542 --> 00:03:34,661
Really?

76
00:03:37,856 --> 00:03:39,176
Yan...

77
00:03:41,674 --> 00:03:42,854
It's still no good

78
00:03:42,894 --> 00:03:44,573
I look completely exhausted

79
00:03:44,613 --> 00:03:46,532
Kentaro, you keep telling me this

80
00:03:46,572 --> 00:03:48,302
What exactly are you getting at?

81
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:50,570
Hey, if you don't feel like drinking

82
00:03:50,610 --> 00:03:52,669
You don't have to join the banquet tonight

83
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:54,029
I'm really sorry

84
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:56,385
That did the trick!

85
00:04:00,854 --> 00:04:03,540
Is Dad coming straight home tonight?

86
00:04:03,581 --> 00:04:05,415
Without a doubt!

87
00:04:08,484 --> 00:04:09,451
It's Dad

88
00:04:09,497 --> 00:04:11,656
Hey, aren't you Kenichi Mitsuba's dad?

89
00:04:11,697 --> 00:04:12,649
Yes, Teacher

90
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:14,508
Wonderful, how about we have a drink together?

91
00:04:14,549 --> 00:04:15,615
That'd be great... wait, huh?

92
00:04:15,971 --> 00:04:17,707
I'd love to have a drink

93
00:04:17,748 --> 00:04:18,924
But unfortunately my complexion is terrible

94
00:04:18,965 --> 00:04:19,972
Not at all!

95
00:04:20,012 --> 00:04:22,515
You're glowing with health, full of energy!

96
00:04:22,635 --> 00:04:24,937
Is that so? Maybe it was all in my head

97
00:04:24,997 --> 00:04:26,151
Let's definitely go have a couple of drinks

98
00:04:26,192 --> 00:04:27,631
Say no more, let's get going

99
00:04:27,888 --> 00:04:29,450
Oh no, Dad...

100
00:04:29,523 --> 00:04:31,170
Old habits really die hard

101
00:04:31,211 --> 00:04:33,611
I must think of a way. Alright

102
00:04:33,932 --> 00:04:35,059
Ninja Shadow Control Technique!

103
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,098
Come on, let's head inside

104
00:04:36,139 --> 00:04:37,032
After you, Teacher

105
00:04:37,077 --> 00:04:38,374
Come on, you go first, no need to stand on ceremony!

106
00:04:38,414 --> 00:04:39,975
Don't mind if I do then

107
00:04:42,257 --> 00:04:43,351
Hey, what's happening?

108
00:04:43,392 --> 00:04:45,739
For some reason my legs suddenly won't move!

109
00:04:45,779 --> 00:04:48,363
Oh... my legs are moving again...

110
00:04:48,404 --> 00:04:50,846
Strange, the shadow is glaring at us?

111
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:52,028
Yan...

112
00:04:52,069 --> 00:04:54,258
Oh no... we're in trouble now!

113
00:04:54,299 --> 00:04:55,206
Run!

114
00:04:55,246 --> 00:04:56,703
Oh, that scared me to death!

115
00:04:56,743 --> 00:04:58,346
Teacher...

116
00:04:58,972 --> 00:05:02,144
Nothing I can do, guess I'll just head home and enjoy a drink

117
00:05:03,583 --> 00:05:04,489
I'm home

118
00:05:04,530 --> 00:05:05,897
-You're back?
-You're back?

119
00:05:05,937 --> 00:05:06,855
You're early today

120
00:05:06,896 --> 00:05:09,418
Yeah, I promised I'd come home early after all

121
00:05:09,459 --> 00:05:11,060
Mom, get me a flask of warm sake

122
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,526
You're drinking again?

123
00:05:12,579 --> 00:05:15,295
Drinking too much is bad for your health

124
00:05:15,422 --> 00:05:18,811
Having you all with me gives drinking a special charm

125
00:05:19,064 --> 00:05:21,025
Dad is truly hopeless

126
00:05:23,583 --> 00:05:25,377
Why is it a sake flask?

127
00:05:27,027 --> 00:05:29,160
It looked just like a sake flask just now

128
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,106
Maybe I've had too much to drink

129
00:05:31,593 --> 00:05:33,598
Ling...

130
00:05:35,797 --> 00:05:37,883
Oh dear... It's another sake flask!

131
00:05:40,648 --> 00:05:42,434
Even hair tonic turned into a sake flask?

132
00:05:42,667 --> 00:05:45,769
I've had too much to drink, my brain's getting affected

133
00:05:50,025 --> 00:05:50,904
Aahh!

134
00:05:50,945 --> 00:05:53,620
How did even my own body turn into a sake flask?

135
00:05:53,918 --> 00:05:55,958
Yan...

136
00:05:57,538 --> 00:05:59,591
Whoa, you scared me!

137
00:06:00,097 --> 00:06:01,806
Here, only one flask, okay?

138
00:06:02,386 --> 00:06:04,301
Another sake flask... I'm not drinking!

139
00:06:04,342 --> 00:06:06,737
No way I'm drinking, I must quit alcohol!

140
00:06:06,777 --> 00:06:08,298
I'll never drink again, aahh!

141
00:06:08,511 --> 00:06:10,957
I'm about to go crazy, this is terrible!

142
00:06:11,659 --> 00:06:14,341
Looks like even Shishimaru can be useful at times

143
00:06:14,381 --> 00:06:16,800
Ling...

144
00:06:17,675 --> 00:06:19,747
Although it was tough on Dad this time

145
00:06:19,787 --> 00:06:23,591
my strategy was a great success, yan...

146
00:06:26,795 --> 00:06:29,763
"Don't Pick Up Lottery Tickets off the Ground"

147
00:06:32,466 --> 00:06:34,073
Alright, the long-awaited...

148
00:06:34,113 --> 00:06:35,833
grand lottery is starting now!

149
00:06:35,873 --> 00:06:37,209
The numbers shot with arrows

150
00:06:37,249 --> 00:06:38,476
by these beautiful ladies

151
00:06:38,516 --> 00:06:39,797
will be the winning numbers!

152
00:06:39,843 --> 00:06:42,740
Let's see which lucky winner gets to vacation in Hawaii!

153
00:06:42,926 --> 00:06:44,008
Here we go!

154
00:06:51,511 --> 00:06:54,615
The results are in, each arrow has a number!

155
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:56,571
And the winning number is...

156
00:06:56,611 --> 00:06:59,987
Nine, zero, two, five!

157
00:07:00,915 --> 00:07:02,306
That's right, the results are out!

158
00:07:02,356 --> 00:07:04,903
It is number 9025!

159
00:07:04,963 --> 00:07:06,198
That's so hard to win

160
00:07:06,238 --> 00:07:07,753
Kemumaki, how did it go?

161
00:07:07,793 --> 00:07:08,879
Didn't win, of course

162
00:07:08,919 --> 00:07:10,640
With so many lottery tickets, only one wins

163
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,561
It really is harder than finding a needle in a haystack

164
00:07:12,601 --> 00:07:15,267
No point wasting time, I'm heading off

165
00:07:15,894 --> 00:07:17,676
There are still other prizes, you know!

166
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,944
Let's try our luck with this ticket first

167
00:07:22,699 --> 00:07:25,265
If we win, we can go to Hawaii!

168
00:07:25,306 --> 00:07:27,298
Can ninjas even go?

169
00:07:27,339 --> 00:07:29,423
Family members can go, silly!

170
00:07:29,463 --> 00:07:30,862
Yan...

171
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:34,445
This ticket is Group A, number 6801

172
00:07:34,712 --> 00:07:36,402
I wonder if it'll win?

173
00:07:37,592 --> 00:07:38,964
Oh, Kemumaki!

174
00:07:39,506 --> 00:07:41,852
The winning numbers are already posted!

175
00:07:41,893 --> 00:07:43,638
They're already posted?

176
00:07:44,522 --> 00:07:46,844
Winning number 6801... 6801...

177
00:07:46,931 --> 00:07:48,251
That number from earlier...

178
00:07:48,292 --> 00:07:50,172
That's right, that's the one!

179
00:07:50,212 --> 00:07:52,895
That's the ticket we threw on the ground earlier!

180
00:07:52,936 --> 00:07:53,929
Go pick it up!

181
00:07:54,036 --> 00:07:56,002
What's Kenichi up to?

182
00:07:56,131 --> 00:07:57,676
None of your business!

183
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:01,852
Found it!

184
00:08:01,892 --> 00:08:03,555
Group A, number 6801!

185
00:08:04,453 --> 00:08:06,773
A trip to Hawaii! Hawaii!

186
00:08:07,814 --> 00:08:08,697
Mom!

187
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,574
Why are you yelling so loudly?

188
00:08:10,614 --> 00:08:12,895
I won a prize for a trip to Hawaii!

189
00:08:12,935 --> 00:08:14,416
I'm really busy right now

190
00:08:14,456 --> 00:08:15,776
A vacation to Hawaii!

191
00:08:15,817 --> 00:08:17,377
We won a prize for a trip to Hawaii!

192
00:08:17,417 --> 00:08:19,017
Really? That's nice then

193
00:08:19,057 --> 00:08:21,223
All right, don't interrupt my work now

194
00:08:24,105 --> 00:08:26,387
Wait a minute, Kenichi, what did you just say?

195
00:08:26,427 --> 00:08:29,070
I said we won a trip to Hawaii!

196
00:08:29,110 --> 00:08:30,898
To Hawaii?

197
00:08:31,712 --> 00:08:32,526
For real?

198
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,752
Are you two teaming up on purpose to trick Mom?

199
00:08:34,793 --> 00:08:36,936
No, it's real, right, Hattori-kun?

200
00:08:37,030 --> 00:08:39,400
Yes, that's what the number says

201
00:08:57,782 --> 00:08:59,162
Mom!

202
00:08:59,246 --> 00:09:00,454
Oh dear, this is bad

203
00:09:00,495 --> 00:09:01,923
My swimsuit is missing!

204
00:09:01,970 --> 00:09:03,971
I have to hurry and buy a new one!

205
00:09:04,532 --> 00:09:06,251
Kenichi, what are you waiting for?

206
00:09:06,291 --> 00:09:08,421
Hurry up and practice your English conversation!

207
00:09:12,957 --> 00:09:13,958
I'm home!

208
00:09:13,998 --> 00:09:16,238
Good evening, Father

209
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,228
Oh, my darling

210
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:19,341
What are you guys doing?

211
00:09:19,382 --> 00:09:21,549
Dad, the department store sale raffle...

212
00:09:21,590 --> 00:09:23,519
We won the grand prize trip to Hawaii!

213
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,900
What did you say?

214
00:09:27,266 --> 00:09:28,539
Yan...

215
00:09:29,376 --> 00:09:31,103
Hattori-kun, you can't do that

216
00:09:31,143 --> 00:09:33,615
Eating like that is bad manners

217
00:09:34,253 --> 00:09:35,894
If you don't get it right

218
00:09:35,935 --> 00:09:38,234
you'll embarrass yourself in Hawaii

219
00:09:38,574 --> 00:09:39,533
Yes

220
00:09:39,573 --> 00:09:42,576
Big Brother, I want to eat with chopsticks

221
00:09:42,617 --> 00:09:43,580
Shinzo

222
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:45,212
We have to learn, you know

223
00:09:45,253 --> 00:09:47,100
Mom, water, please

224
00:09:47,533 --> 00:09:49,259
Your English is terrible

225
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,542
I meant, "Please give me some water"

226
00:09:50,582 --> 00:09:52,102
OK, my darling

227
00:09:52,142 --> 00:09:53,343
Yan...

228
00:09:56,779 --> 00:09:58,563
OK, my darling

229
00:09:59,107 --> 00:10:01,101
They really think being cheesy is cute

230
00:10:03,507 --> 00:10:04,241
Hattori-kun

231
00:10:04,281 --> 00:10:06,333
I heard you're getting to go to Hawaii too, is that true?

232
00:10:06,374 --> 00:10:08,634
First, let me wish you a pleasant journey

233
00:10:10,889 --> 00:10:12,232
Something fishy is definitely going on

234
00:10:12,273 --> 00:10:14,439
Could Kemumaki be playing tricks?

235
00:10:16,895 --> 00:10:18,429
Number 9025

236
00:10:18,469 --> 00:10:20,135
Oh dear, it really is

237
00:10:20,499 --> 00:10:22,301
Oh dear, I just packed away the summer clothes

238
00:10:22,341 --> 00:10:24,198
and now I have to take them all out again

239
00:10:24,365 --> 00:10:26,412
Hi, Mr. Ninja

240
00:10:26,452 --> 00:10:28,344
Kenichi, come over here

241
00:10:28,697 --> 00:10:31,033
What? Winning the trip to Hawaii is fake?

242
00:10:31,074 --> 00:10:32,426
I was really too careless

243
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:34,586
Oh dear, let's solve this with ninjutsu

244
00:10:34,626 --> 00:10:35,630
Yan...

245
00:10:35,984 --> 00:10:38,586
Dad, can you take time off from work?

246
00:10:38,627 --> 00:10:40,752
Oh, I have plenty of vacation days

247
00:10:41,071 --> 00:10:44,190
All right, Ninja Illusion to Reality Technique, yan!

248
00:10:49,626 --> 00:10:51,664
Whoa, it's so heavy

249
00:10:51,704 --> 00:10:53,697
Around here should be good enough

250
00:10:53,738 --> 00:10:55,163
It should work out as planned

251
00:10:55,249 --> 00:10:57,313
Kenichi, you have to help Mom out

252
00:10:57,353 --> 00:10:58,281
Okay

253
00:11:02,904 --> 00:11:04,371
Dad, you're finally awake?

254
00:11:04,745 --> 00:11:06,186
Why am I here?

255
00:11:06,226 --> 00:11:07,787
Because it was so late and you hadn't come home

256
00:11:07,827 --> 00:11:09,968
so I came looking for you

257
00:11:10,281 --> 00:11:11,549
What on earth are you talking about?

258
00:11:11,589 --> 00:11:12,780
Aren't you going back quickly?

259
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,271
I need to pack for Hawaii

260
00:11:14,311 --> 00:11:15,256
Hawaii?

261
00:11:15,376 --> 00:11:17,563
Yeah, we won first prize to Hawaii, remember?

262
00:11:17,604 --> 00:11:18,874
How come I haven't heard about this?

263
00:11:18,914 --> 00:11:20,475
Were you dreaming?

264
00:11:21,596 --> 00:11:22,995
What? You're saying I was dreaming?

265
00:11:23,035 --> 00:11:24,154
Yeah, it was a dream

266
00:11:24,194 --> 00:11:26,813
How could we be so lucky to win?

267
00:11:26,854 --> 00:11:28,794
But Dad was just packing with me earlier

268
00:11:28,834 --> 00:11:30,606
Huh? Dad hasn't even come home yet

269
00:11:30,746 --> 00:11:34,463
If it was a dream, it was way too realistic

270
00:11:34,633 --> 00:11:36,632
Dad, that was a nice dream, wasn't it?

271
00:11:36,672 --> 00:11:37,977
Yeah, it's so embarrassing

272
00:11:38,017 --> 00:11:39,335
Don't tell Mom

273
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:41,661
I really am ridiculous

274
00:11:41,708 --> 00:11:43,916
I even bought a swimsuit in the dream

275
00:11:43,957 --> 00:11:45,230
You bought a swimsuit?

276
00:11:45,428 --> 00:11:46,165
I'm home

277
00:11:46,212 --> 00:11:47,569
Oh, Dad is back

278
00:11:47,722 --> 00:11:50,557
Kenichi, don't tell Dad about my dream

279
00:11:51,105 --> 00:11:52,877
If we hadn't picked up this ticket, none of this would've happened

280
00:11:52,923 --> 00:11:55,275
Good thing the problem was resolved in time

281
00:11:55,316 --> 00:11:56,560
Hurry up and tear it up

282
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:59,251
Don't be so hasty, we just didn't win first prize

283
00:11:59,292 --> 00:12:01,642
Maybe we won another prize

284
00:12:03,984 --> 00:12:05,810
Now, for Group A...

285
00:12:06,056 --> 00:12:07,575
Number 6801 also wins a big prize

286
00:12:07,616 --> 00:12:09,576
The prize is a brand-new bicycle!

287
00:12:10,717 --> 00:12:12,629
Hattori-kun, we really won a prize!

288
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:14,266
Kenichi, congratulations!

289
00:12:14,306 --> 00:12:15,300
Oh no, this is terrible

290
00:12:15,341 --> 00:12:17,881
I gave away the prize for nothing!

291
00:12:18,026 --> 00:12:20,302
Kemumaki really let a golden opportunity slip away

292
00:12:20,343 --> 00:12:21,933
Yan...

293
00:12:24,341 --> 00:12:26,773
"Ninja Blizzard"

294
00:12:28,738 --> 00:12:31,338
Kenichi, hurry up and get up to see

295
00:12:31,458 --> 00:12:33,632
Oh, I still want to sleep

296
00:12:33,678 --> 00:12:36,012
Stop sleeping, hurry up and see this

297
00:12:36,859 --> 00:12:38,529
What is there to see?

298
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:40,498
Get up and look, and you'll know

299
00:12:40,538 --> 00:12:42,144
Get up quickly

300
00:12:42,278 --> 00:12:43,953
What on earth is there to see?

301
00:12:43,994 --> 00:12:45,595
Look outside

302
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:52,846
So fun!

303
00:12:52,887 --> 00:12:54,367
So fun!

304
00:12:55,903 --> 00:12:57,908
-Here it comes!
-This is so fun!

305
00:12:58,369 --> 00:13:00,234
Wow, it's Hattori-kun and the others!

306
00:13:01,495 --> 00:13:02,496
Oh no, Mom!

307
00:13:02,536 --> 00:13:05,075
Why didn't you wake me up earlier?

308
00:13:05,339 --> 00:13:07,508
If the snow melts, I'm holding you responsible!

309
00:13:07,935 --> 00:13:10,669
Kenichi, change your clothes before you go out!

310
00:13:18,635 --> 00:13:20,430
Look, there's my face!

311
00:13:20,471 --> 00:13:22,037
Doing this is so fun

312
00:13:22,077 --> 00:13:23,709
I must try it too

313
00:13:23,749 --> 00:13:25,231
I want to try it too!

314
00:13:28,662 --> 00:13:31,238
Ow, that hurts so much!

315
00:13:35,110 --> 00:13:38,710
Listen up, whoever leaves the most footprints in the snow wins!

317
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:40,230
-Did you hear that?
-I know what to do!

318
00:13:40,270 --> 00:13:41,310
Hurry up and start!

319
00:13:41,350 --> 00:13:42,990
Alright, let's start!

320
00:14:00,241 --> 00:14:02,534
Man, beating them really isn't easy!

321
00:14:02,589 --> 00:14:03,556
Awesome, awesome!

322
00:14:03,596 --> 00:14:05,610
I have just as many footprints as Big Brother!

323
00:14:05,650 --> 00:14:06,892
Are you kidding me?

324
00:14:06,932 --> 00:14:08,648
How could you possibly be as good as me?

325
00:14:08,688 --> 00:14:11,367
Alright, now let's start making snowmen!

326
00:14:11,407 --> 00:14:12,812
Huh? Make snowmen?

327
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:15,232
Whatever it is, a ninja never loses!

328
00:14:15,273 --> 00:14:17,158
I don't want to compete this time

329
00:14:17,199 --> 00:14:19,792
First, we need to make a big snowball

330
00:14:21,392 --> 00:14:22,816
Yan...

331
00:14:23,542 --> 00:14:24,522
Hey, Hattori-kun!

332
00:14:24,563 --> 00:14:26,427
-What is it?
-Ow... What's wrong?

333
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:27,910
Hey, hurry up and help out

334
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:29,797
What are you just standing there for? Hurry up!

335
00:14:29,897 --> 00:14:32,197
Make a snowball? You want me to make a snowball?

336
00:14:32,237 --> 00:14:33,191
Alright

337
00:14:34,521 --> 00:14:35,804
I'm fine now

338
00:14:37,343 --> 00:14:39,451
It's the Ninja Snowball Rolling Technique!

339
00:14:39,492 --> 00:14:40,452
Yan...

340
00:14:40,706 --> 00:14:41,936
Awesome!

341
00:14:41,995 --> 00:14:43,752
Hey, let me try!

342
00:14:44,043 --> 00:14:45,610
It looks so fun, I want to try too!

343
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:47,491
Kenichi, go right ahead and try!

344
00:14:47,531 --> 00:14:50,750
Alright! Ow...

345
00:14:50,856 --> 00:14:52,388
Oh no, Kenichi!

346
00:14:58,496 --> 00:14:59,901
All finished!

347
00:15:00,783 --> 00:15:03,361
-Yay, awesome!
-It's all done!

348
00:15:03,670 --> 00:15:05,953
On the left is Yumeko, and on the right is Kenichi!

349
00:15:05,993 --> 00:15:07,954
It shows just how well-matched you two are!

350
00:15:10,558 --> 00:15:13,481
Wow, Kenichi and Yumeko really get along great

351
00:15:13,521 --> 00:15:16,175
They're really good friends, aren't they?

352
00:15:16,365 --> 00:15:18,549
Uh... it's just a coincidence

353
00:15:18,877 --> 00:15:20,904
Alright, now let's start a snowball fight!

354
00:15:21,524 --> 00:15:23,524
Okay, don't run away!

355
00:15:24,391 --> 00:15:25,767
Oh, Boss!

356
00:15:25,808 --> 00:15:28,563
In this cold weather, we really should be by the fireplace

357
00:15:28,603 --> 00:15:31,002
Let's just head home early, okay?

358
00:15:31,043 --> 00:15:31,873
Stop whining!

359
00:15:31,914 --> 00:15:34,305
Plenty of animals love the snow, you know

360
00:15:34,346 --> 00:15:36,799
That might be true for dogs, but we cats hate the cold!

361
00:15:36,888 --> 00:15:38,574
I'm shivering so much from the cold

362
00:15:39,234 --> 00:15:40,701
It'll be a miracle if I don't catch a cold

363
00:15:41,236 --> 00:15:43,120
Stop nagging, I told you!

364
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:45,080
Hurry up and follow Big Boss!

365
00:15:47,749 --> 00:15:50,681
Huh? Kenichi is actually with Yumeko?!

366
00:15:50,722 --> 00:15:53,089
Darn it, curse him!

367
00:15:53,349 --> 00:15:55,444
Ninja Thunderbolt Kick Technique!

368
00:15:58,756 --> 00:16:00,196
All done!

369
00:16:06,363 --> 00:16:08,765
All right... I'm not playing anymore, I quit!

370
00:16:08,806 --> 00:16:10,980
Kenichi, why quit so soon?

371
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:12,261
We were having so much fun just now

372
00:16:12,301 --> 00:16:13,583
I don't think it's fun at all

373
00:16:13,623 --> 00:16:15,385
Because all three of you know ninja magic

374
00:16:15,425 --> 00:16:17,442
I have no chance of beating you

375
00:16:17,542 --> 00:16:19,985
All right, then during our snowball fight...

376
00:16:20,025 --> 00:16:21,112
we won't use ninja magic

377
00:16:21,152 --> 00:16:22,904
That would be fair, wouldn't it?

378
00:16:22,945 --> 00:16:23,832
Really?

379
00:16:23,872 --> 00:16:25,779
You mean it! No using magic, okay?

380
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:26,899
Don't forget that!

381
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:29,745
Yan... I give you my word, I won't go back on it

382
00:16:30,778 --> 00:16:34,695
Ling...

383
00:16:36,647 --> 00:16:39,230
Oh no, someone ruined it?

384
00:16:39,285 --> 00:16:40,676
- Brother!
- Oh dear, what is it?

385
00:16:41,546 --> 00:16:44,393
Ruining my head? What's the meaning of this?

386
00:16:44,433 --> 00:16:46,991
Who could do something so cowardly?

387
00:16:48,333 --> 00:16:49,526
Who is it?

388
00:16:50,596 --> 00:16:51,838
Where are you hiding?

389
00:16:53,491 --> 00:16:55,325
Over there!

390
00:16:57,026 --> 00:16:58,136
Over there!

391
00:17:02,933 --> 00:17:04,165
Help...

392
00:17:04,205 --> 00:17:05,893
Hattori-kun, save me!

393
00:17:06,405 --> 00:17:09,244
Kenichi, can I use ninja magic now?

394
00:17:09,284 --> 00:17:12,324
Of course you can, hurry up and use it!

395
00:17:12,364 --> 00:17:13,853
That's great, then!

396
00:17:14,003 --> 00:17:16,613
Here's the Ninja Blizzard Technique!

397
00:17:20,428 --> 00:17:21,965
Yan...

398
00:17:26,994 --> 00:17:28,188
I knew it was Kemumaki!

399
00:17:28,228 --> 00:17:30,108
I'm going to teach you a lesson, watch out!

400
00:17:30,148 --> 00:17:31,414
Yan...

401
00:17:37,610 --> 00:17:38,700
It worked!

402
00:17:38,740 --> 00:17:39,651
Yan... Oh no...

403
00:17:39,751 --> 00:17:41,287
You think you can catch me, Hattori-kun?

404
00:17:41,327 --> 00:17:43,062
It won't be that easy!

405
00:17:43,322 --> 00:17:45,881
Who knew there was such a bizarre technique?

406
00:17:57,289 --> 00:17:58,162
How's that, huh?

407
00:17:58,203 --> 00:18:00,846
Now you should know how tough it is being a snowman

408
00:18:00,886 --> 00:18:02,774
How's that for impressive, huh?

409
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,324
Confound it!

410
00:18:05,810 --> 00:18:08,443
Turns out you two look so nice

411
00:18:08,637 --> 00:18:10,964
So cute, just like ice cream!

412
00:18:11,004 --> 00:18:13,409
Damn it! Let me go already!

413
00:18:13,449 --> 00:18:15,733
Oh dear, I told you from the start I hate snow!

414
00:18:15,774 --> 00:18:17,247
Now we're really in for it

